TITLE:: ToggleSwitch
summary:: A nice little Toggle switch
categories:: GUI>Views
related:: Classes/Button, Classes/SCViewHolder

DESCRIPTION::
A horizontal or vertical toggle switch with a label

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
create a new ToggleSwitch.

ARGUMENT:: parent
A parent view.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
A Rect. if width>height, a horizontal switch, otherwise vertical.

ARGUMENT:: label
A label text. For vertical swiches omit or make very short.

ARGUMENT:: toggleSize
The size of the toggle widget (width or height).

ARGUMENT:: label2
An optional second label on the other side of the switch.

ARGUMENT:: radius
a radius size for corners. defualts to \auto .

returns:: a new ToggleSwitch

METHOD:: newSquare
a convencienc method to create a ToggleSwitch with no rouding or button inset.
returns:: a new ToggleSwitch

METHOD:: defaultOnColor
default:Color.green(0.6);

override individually with onColor

METHOD:: defaultOffColor
default: Color.grey.alpha_(0.6);

override individually with offColor


INSTANCEMETHODS::
All of the setter  methods except value and valueAction need you to do myInstance.view.refresh after setting the value;

